# Loose ends

Small things that came up while other work was going on. Written down in the turn they come up,
drained after an order resolves, at each checkpoint, and on request ("drain the loose ends").
This list is the one place "not now" lives: every item that is not yet an order is one row here.

Only the orchestrator writes it (`scripts/loose_ends.py`). An item is one or two sentences, at most
300 characters. This is never a work queue or a notebook: a finding that needs evidence, a cause, a
fix or its own worker is a work-order; a session plan belongs in `RESUME.md`. State is one of
`new`, `proposed: <kind>` (the drain's; its file in `drain/pending/` is an attachment),
`parked: <trigger>`, `waiting: <question>` or `declined: <reason>`. A routed or closed item is
removed with `drop --to WO-NNN | WO-NNN/SN | brain:<page> | closed:<reason>` and git keeps the
history: not on the list means routed.

